WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.190
 This is not juggling.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.510
This is called misdirection.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.450
And no matter what
level you are magic,

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.490
we've got stuff here for you.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.350
Learning basic
principles of magic,

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:16.210
it's like learning
chords on a guitar.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.190
Once you know a few
simple principles,

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:22.231
you can build your
whole magic routine.

00:00:22.231 --> 00:00:25.360
But if you're smart
enough to work silently,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.300
it brings out a huge
amount of wonder.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.380
 When you don't
talk, the audience

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.120
has to tell itself
the story, and they

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.870
don't know where it's going.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.990
The basic method behind this
uses sound misdirection.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:44.954
[COINS JINGLING]

00:00:44.954 --> 00:00:48.330
[COUGH]

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.497
Palming is when you hide
something in your hand.

00:00:50.497 --> 00:00:52.330
You're going to bring
your whole hand around

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.990
to conceal that ball and
completely close your fist.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:03.610
That will make all
your relatives laugh.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.150
 The simplest trick you
can do involves exploring

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:10.210
how do we know what is true.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.980
 Take those two
ends and tie them

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.050
in a double knot
around each other.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.191
Yeah, I'll see you later.

00:01:15.191 --> 00:01:17.900
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.560
 There's more magic in
cards than anything else.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.240
You don't need to know the card.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.875
You just need to know the
card next to the card.

00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:26.750
 Was that your card?

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:26.985
 Whoa

00:01:26.985 --> 00:01:27.692
 Yes.

00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:30.518
[LAUGHTER]

00:01:32.873 --> 00:01:36.120
If you get good at magic, you
will automatically get good

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.410
at a certain kind of acting.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.310
 Magic forces you to learn
about storytelling, assumptions

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.770
about the way we
perceive the world.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.250
 And then smash it.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:45.750
That's it.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.490
 You must be empathetic.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.490
You must try to see yourself
through another person's eyes,

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:53.280
and I think you
have to simply say

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.370
that one of the things that
makes life worth living

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.620
is giving other people joy.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:06.690
We're Penn and Teller, and
this is our MasterClass.

